    "rich_text_BceXEC": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_twNKDt": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Ivory Candles FAQ",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "heading_font_class": "fs-heading-2-base"
          }
        },
        "border_YXYC4e": {
          "type": "border",
          "settings": {}
        },
        "subheading_CQxqUm": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What is the best place to start if I know I want ivory candles but have not chosen the format yet?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-5-base"
          }
        },
        "text_Yp3wdG": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Start with the part of the room you need to light first. If you need candles for holders, begin with ivory tapers; if you need fuller centerpieces or tabletop groupings, begin with ivory pillars; if you need bowls or water-based arrangements, begin with ivory floating candles.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_Gyn8i7": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_7VFPF8": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How do I choose between ivory pillars, ivory tapers, and ivory floating candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-5-base"
          }
        },
        "text_chD3GE": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose ivory pillars when you want more body and presence on the table, choose ivory tapers when the setup depends on holders and a cleaner vertical line, and choose ivory floating candles when the arrangement is built around water and glass. The right format comes from the display style first and the color second.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_ErYGDn": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_DxgNe6": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are the ivory candles in this collection unscented?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-5-base"
          }
        },
        "text_bgNUHe": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, these ivory candles are unscented. That makes them a practical choice for dining tables, events, and decorative use when you want candlelight without adding fragrance to the room.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_3QNkWm": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_6rLawb": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What is the easiest way to keep the ivory tone consistent across different candle styles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-5-base"
          }
        },
        "text_bEKLHA": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose your pillars, tapers, and floating candles from the same ivory assortment instead of mixing similar shades from different sources. Kisco Candles keeps this collection within the Bolsius ivory line, which makes it much easier to build a room around a single ivory tone.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_xd3bqj": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_BfC4MW": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which ivory candles work best for a formal dining table?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-5-base"
          }
        },
        "text_FfNFXM": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Ivory tapers usually work best for a formal dining table because they pair naturally with candleholders and create a cleaner, more traditional candle line. The ivory range here includes 7\", 9\", 10\", and 11.5\" tapers, so the look can stay consistent even when the table style changes.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_9FNeye": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_b4aeYi": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which ivory candles work best for a fuller centerpiece without tall holders?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-5-base"
          }
        },
        "text_fByHn8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Ivory pillars usually work best for that job because they bring more shape and visual weight to the arrangement on their own. Kisco Candles assortment includes classic pillar packs, grouped pillar sizes, and wider pillar options, so it is easier to build a fuller centerpiece in one ivory tone.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_tX6naQ": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_4LDb7L": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How can I use more than one ivory candle style in the same room without the décor feeling repetitive?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-5-base"
          }
        },
        "text_mfVCJQ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Give each style a clear role. A strong approach is to use ivory tapers on dining tables, ivory pillars in grouped decorative areas, and ivory floating candles in glass vessels or accent spots so the room stays coordinated without looking copied from table to table.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        }
      },
